description:
Lines 286-289 in watch.rs treat HTTP 401 and 403 the same:
  if status_code == 403 || status_code == 401 {
    eprintln!(...'not recognized as owner'...)
    return Ok(());
  }

The status codes have different meanings:
- 401 Unauthorized: client didn't send credentials (wrong identity)  
- 403 Forbidden: credentials sent but explicitly rejected (blacklisted/blocked)

Both lead to clean exit, which is correct, but the error message is misleading for 403. No doc comment explains the distinction.

SUGGESTION: Either document why both codes are treated the same, or provide more specific error messages per status code.
